<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Workers' Party of Ethiopia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1984–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Workers' Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> was the Marxist–Leninist ruling party founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> military regime in 1984, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu Haile Mariam</a> as general secretary. Under the constitution of 1987 it became the leading force of the People's Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, and it collapsed when rebel forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/workers-party-of-ethiopia.jpg" alt="Workers' Party of Ethiopia" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Workers_Party_of_Ethiopia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
